---
import NumberInput from '../../components/ui/NumberInput.astro';
import RangeInput from '../../components/ui/RangeInput.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Range" code={'<RangeInput id="volume" name="volume" label="Volume" value={40} />\n<RangeInput id="steps" name="steps" label="…" min={0} max={10} step={1} value={7} />'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
        <p>A slider for an approximate value within a range. It's the native range input with its track and thumb redrawn: the track before the thumb fills with the primary colour, and the thumb is ringed in the surface colour. Drag it, or use the arrow, Page Up/Down and Home/End keys.</p>
        <p>The fill follows the thumb without script. When the exact number matters, pair the slider with a number input or use one alone.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <div class="form">
        <RangeInput id="ranges-volume" name="volume" label="Volume" value={40} />
        <RangeInput id="ranges-steps" name="steps" label="Detail level" min={0} max={10} step={1} value={7} help="From 0 (least) to 10 (most)." />
        <RangeInput id="ranges-start" name="start" label="At the minimum" value={0} />
        <RangeInput id="ranges-end" name="end" label="At the maximum" value={100} />
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Range states" code={'<RangeInput … error="…" />\n<RangeInput … disabled />'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>An error replaces the help text and edges the track in the danger colour. Disabled sliders are dimmed.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="form">
        <RangeInput id="ranges-invalid" name="invalid" label="Budget" value={90} error="Choose a value of 80 or less." />
        <RangeInput id="ranges-disabled" name="disabled" label="Disabled" value={30} disabled />
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Number input" code={'<NumberInput id="quantity" name="quantity" label="Quantity" min={1} max={99} value={1} />'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes">
        <p>A field for an exact number. As in Stride, the browser's spinner buttons are hidden, so it reads as a plain field; the up and down arrow keys still step the value by <code>step</code>, within <code>min</code> and <code>max</code>, and touch devices show a numeric keyboard.</p>
        <p>Use it for quantities and measurements, not for identifiers like phone or card numbers, which aren't numbers to count with: use a text input for those.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <div class="form">
        <NumberInput id="ranges-quantity" name="quantity" label="Quantity" min={1} max={99} value={1} />
        <NumberInput id="ranges-amount" name="amount" label="Amount" min={0} step={0.01} placeholder="0.00" help="In US dollars, to the cent." />
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Number input states" code={'<NumberInput … required error="…" />\n<NumberInput … disabled />'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The shared field states: an error replaces the help text and turns the border to the danger colour, and disabled fields drop to the alternate surface.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="form">
        <NumberInput id="ranges-seats" name="seats" label="Seats" min={1} max={20} value={25} required error="Enter a number from 1 to 20." />
        <NumberInput id="ranges-number-disabled" name="number-disabled" label="Disabled" value={12} disabled />
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="On a dark band" surface="dark">
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The same controls inside a near-black band in light mode.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="form">
        <RangeInput id="ranges-dark-range" name="dark-range" label="Volume" value={60} />
        <RangeInput id="ranges-dark-disabled" name="dark-disabled" label="Disabled" value={20} disabled />
        <NumberInput id="ranges-dark-number" name="dark-number" label="Quantity" min={1} value={3} />
    </div>
</Specimen>

<style>
    .form {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        max-width: 32rem;
    }
</style>
